    "reviews": {
      "umvpa-wave3-independent-review-20260930": {
        "body": "Approve corrected M2.03 candidate b4f3ccdf929de5aeb3f0dcbb1bafab547fcb804f. No remaining blocking findings in the reviewed M2 scope. I reviewed the implementation and the mathematical expectations and code of independently authored oracles; I inspected retained execution receipts and did not execute these builds.\n\nThe prior coordinate-variance defect is repaired: CrossClosure[L,R] is Lin[Primal[R],Dual[L]], first-order contrasts are Lin[Primal[E],Primal[C]], and all intermediate boundaries compose through public Lin.andThen. QueryEvaluation is removed. Scalar evaluation traces an endomorphism of Dual[ER] in width-one batches. Tests reject same-axis Table closures, dual forms and old contrast witnesses, admit public primal forms through actual query evaluation, and retain signed rectangular, reversal, actual-adjoint, replay-refusal, lazy-access and scale-aware independent numerical checks.\n\nVerified clean canonical HEAD b4f3ccdf929de5aeb3f0dcbb1bafab547fcb804f and exact M2 blob parity with mixed 6e8aacdbcea18b4b75bd1058f3747815d8b75b9b: Queries.scala 933223314f9138bd7d030f553d4192e6f2680adb; QueryOracleSuite.scala be5b2ee11d462d8c72f1b4ee5d09d8e10c624f60; verification document 6e2fee41e24690d715fbd16958acec809cd737ec.\n\nFresh corrected-source receipts: variance-canonical-jvm-compile.log contains mvpaJVM/test 209 passed, zero failed/errors, then scalafimCompileAll; its metadata records exit_code=0 and child_returncode=0. variance-canonical-js-final.log contains mvpaJS/test 209 passed, zero failed/errors, and metadata exit_code=0 and child_returncode=0. Full logs were scanned, byte lengths match metadata, and neither has any warn/error lines. Log SHA256 respectively d89ba7b4d84d4f5dbef7fcf22cb4a157716e097a2a998797332a498b4a05d10e and 0a516753615f5fa9f5e6281b6758729bee71276185da6f932b2e3e8d7a851b30.\n\nSource review and fresh receipt paths:\n/private/tmp/scalafim-umvpa-20260930-wave3-evidence/independent-review-final.md\n/private/tmp/scalafim-umvpa-20260930-wave3-evidence/variance-canonical-jvm-compile.log\n/private/tmp/scalafim-umvpa-20260930-wave3-evidence/variance-canonical-jvm-compile.log.meta.json\n/private/tmp/scalafim-umvpa-20260930-wave3-evidence/variance-canonical-js-final.log\n/private/tmp/scalafim-umvpa-20260930-wave3-evidence/variance-canonical-js-final.log.meta.json\n\nThis approval applies to the corrected immutable candidate; it does not restore approval of the superseded 4f52 candidate. Native adapter source was not re-reviewed in this bounded operation. No landing authorization, landing, ancestor resolution, upstream Alder publication or immutable pin qualification is granted by this review.",
